From bf4f319f9d35ea204071ae97f3844be9c5ae7bf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "jian.wang04" <jian.wang04@united-imaging.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:18:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] add MXFP4 -> FP8 expert checkpoint conversion for SM90

Hopper (SM90, e.g. H20) has no FP4 tensor cores, so the released MXFP4
checkpoint cannot run there. scripts/convert_mxfp4_to_fp8.py rewrites the
routed experts (packed e2m1 + per-row UE8M0 scales) into F8_E4M3 with
per-32x32-block FP32 scales, copies everything else byte-identically, and
flips config.json to expert_dtype=fp8 (+ use_fp4_sparse_kv=false). It
needs only torch and safetensors, so it runs on a CPU box.

config.py now accepts expert_dtype 'fp8' alongside 'fp4'; the runtime
fp8xfp8 MoE path already exists (mlp.py process_moe_weight use_fp4=False),
so the remaining gap is the FP8-expert branch in _load_expert_params.
